{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TkrxgHNf3aPCBi8CFVHLFx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about CoRL 2026 instructions for authors and some reviewer-related requirements, but I did not find a specific dedicated \"CoRL 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\" or \"Review Form\" document yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Author Reviewer Requirements\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## General Review Expectations\nThe conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. The search results did reference ICML and NeurIPS guidance on constructive reviewing, which CoRL's guidelines build upon.\n\nThe search results included information from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but I did not locate the complete CoRL 2026 Reviewer Guidelines or Review Form document. These materials may not yet be publicly available or may be accessible only through the OpenReview platform directly. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) or contact the CoRL organizers for the most current reviewer guidelines and review form.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53be8891-6c2e-4099-b6c6-0858d8cae474","uuid":"e89e81c4-1c04-400d-8994-41961ddbed1f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:48:57.802Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WHUq6mJTrMCpkmc8egeXGB","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"}]},"Based on my search results, I found information about CoRL 2026 instructions for authors and some reviewer-related requirements, but I did not find a specific dedicated \"CoRL 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\" or \"Review Form\" document yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Author Reviewer Requirements\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## General Review Expectations\nThe conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. The search results did reference ICML and NeurIPS guidance on constructive reviewing, which CoRL's guidelines build upon.\n\nThe search results included information from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but I did not locate the complete CoRL 2026 Reviewer Guidelines or Review Form document. These materials may not yet be publicly available or may be accessible only through the OpenReview platform directly. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) or contact the CoRL organizers for the most current reviewer guidelines and review form."],"durationSeconds":6.085288148}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KVDPvJ14FKjXqpCLTNhP7w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]\",\"url\":\"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL, though the results don't contain comprehensive details specifically about CoRL 2025's scoring rubric or acceptance rate. Here's what I found:\n\n**Reviewer Guidelines:**\nICML and NeurIPS provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews, and CoRL's guidelines build on these resources. The search results reference the CoRL review process being about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period, but don't provide specific details about the 2025 scoring rubric itself.\n\n**Limitations Section:**\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors, which should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results don't contain specific information about:\n- CoRL 2025's detailed scoring rubric with specific score values\n- The 2025 acceptance rate\n\nThe search results reference Paper Copilot which tracks CoRL statistics, which might have more detailed acceptance rate information, but the specific data wasn't included in these results. For the most current and detailed information about CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring, I'd recommend checking the official OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 or the conference's official website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53be8891-6c2e-4099-b6c6-0858d8cae474","uuid":"d88f2454-91e7-4949-a845-a856bcceadd5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:49:03.368Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WerVVVoa7pj9b363DzE3Sc","content":[{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]","url":"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL, though the results don't contain comprehensive details specifically about CoRL 2025's scoring rubric or acceptance rate. Here's what I found:\n\n**Reviewer Guidelines:**\nICML and NeurIPS provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews, and CoRL's guidelines build on these resources. The search results reference the CoRL review process being about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period, but don't provide specific details about the 2025 scoring rubric itself.\n\n**Limitations Section:**\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors, which should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results don't contain specific information about:\n- CoRL 2025's detailed scoring rubric with specific score values\n- The 2025 acceptance rate\n\nThe search results reference Paper Copilot which tracks CoRL statistics, which might have more detailed acceptance rate information, but the specific data wasn't included in these results. For the most current and detailed information about CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring, I'd recommend checking the official OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 or the conference's official website directly."],"durationSeconds":11.572729473999999}}
