{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013n6cK8HDx4M18ttF2yeS6v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale overall score novelty significance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://virtual.aistats.org/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Conference on Robot Learning\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/corl_conf/status/1666663426339508224\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. However, the search results don't contain the specific rating scale details you're looking for. The CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page does mention key evaluation criteria, but the specific numerical rating scale for overall score, novelty, and significance isn't fully detailed in these search results.\n\nFrom what I found, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines ask reviewers to assess relevance by considering whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nAdditionally, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and reflected strongly in scores.\n\nTo get the specific rating scale details for overall score, novelty, and significance metrics for CoRL 2023, you may need to access the full CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page directly at corl2023.org, as those specific numerical scales weren't captured in the available search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53be8891-6c2e-4099-b6c6-0858d8cae474","uuid":"952e2579-aeb8-425a-be59-1720e0dc4e25","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:49:13.625Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale overall score novelty significance","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0133NEEoNUFLjNV19Buvd2Uz","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://virtual.aistats.org/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference"},{"title":"Conference on Robot Learning","url":"https://twitter.com/corl_conf/status/1666663426339508224"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. However, the search results don't contain the specific rating scale details you're looking for. The CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page does mention key evaluation criteria, but the specific numerical rating scale for overall score, novelty, and significance isn't fully detailed in these search results.\n\nFrom what I found, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines ask reviewers to assess relevance by considering whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nAdditionally, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and reflected strongly in scores.\n\nTo get the specific rating scale details for overall score, novelty, and significance metrics for CoRL 2023, you may need to access the full CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page directly at corl2023.org, as those specific numerical scales weren't captured in the available search results."],"durationSeconds":5.6822736069999955}}
