s\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page, but the detailed scoring scale (1-10) and specific review form criteria weren't fully displayed in the search excerpts. The search results show information about review criteria, desk rejection processes, and reviewer requirements, but not the complete scoring rubric with the 1-10 scale definitions.\n\nThe information I found indicates that submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, the specific scoring scale guidance (1-10) and detailed form criteria you're looking for don't appear to be fully captured in the search results. To access the complete review form with the full 1-10 scoring scale criteria, you may need to:\n\n1. Visit the official page directly at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\n2. Check the OpenReview platform (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference) where the review forms are typically hosted\n3. Contact the CoRL 2024 organizers directly for the complete reviewer guidelines\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53be8891-6c2e-4099-b6c6-0858d8cae474","uuid":"2253841a-bb8e-4b36-8f4b-4a96b67e6405","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:49:19.460Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale 1-10 review form criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_